# Auth & Security Rules

## Token Storage — httpOnly Cookie, NOT localStorage (C1)
Tokens **must never be stored in `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`**. The server sets httpOnly, secure cookies. The PWA uses `credentials: 'include'` and never sends `Authorization: Bearer`.

## Logout Is a Server Round-Trip (C3)
`POST /api/auth/logout` expires the cookie. Clearing React state is not logout.

## Short-Lived Access + Refresh (C4)
Two cookies. Revocation is server-side.

## Vault plaintext never hits the API (C5)
Encrypt in the browser. The API stores `Bytes` ciphertext only. Do not return `passwordHash`, wrapped keys, or ciphertext in logs.
